Open_Mouse - third-party notices

Open_Mouse's own code has no licence yet (to be decided; see README.md).

This file lists third-party material that Open_Mouse redistributes: files
vendored in this repository, and npm packages that ship in the deployed app.
It records what was verified and where. Anything that could not be confirmed
says "Unconfirmed". It is not legal advice.

Last checked: 2026-09-30.


1. Vendored files: public/mediapipe/
====================================

1.1 MediaPipe Tasks Vision runtime (WebAssembly)

  Files:    wasm/vision_wasm_internal.js and .wasm      (SIMD build)
            wasm/vision_wasm_nosimd_internal.js and .wasm
                                                        (fallback for browsers
                                                        without WebAssembly SIMD)
  Origin:   npm package @mediapipe/tasks-vision 1.0.1, copied unmodified
            (byte-identical; SHA-256 digests in public/mediapipe/README.md).
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0.
  Evidence: "license": "Apache-2.0" in the package's package.json and in
            package-lock.json; the upstream repository
            https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe declares Apache
            License 2.0 (its LICENSE is copied to
            public/mediapipe/LICENSE-mediapipe.txt).
  Not found: the npm package contains no LICENSE or NOTICE file of its own.

  Statically linked code - Unconfirmed. The .wasm files are static builds. A
  string search of the binary finds code from other projects: Abseil,
  Protocol Buffers, XNNPACK, TensorFlow Lite, ruy, gemmlowp, Eigen, OpenCV,
  FlatBuffers and the Emscripten runtime. The package ships no notices for
  them, and which versions and licence terms are compiled in was not confirmed.

  Usage metrics. The package README's privacy notice (last modified
  2026-06-05) says the Tasks APIs send performance and usage metrics to
  Google, and that input data such as images is processed on the device and
  not sent to Google. The bundle contains the logger (endpoint
  https://odml.pa.googleapis.com/v1/log). Open_Mouse's Content-Security-Policy
  (connect-src 'self', next.config.ts) blocks that request: observed on
  2026-09-30 in Chromium against the dev server, the browser logged
  "Refused to connect ... because it violates the document's Content Security
  Policy" and no request left the page. Loosening connect-src would let it
  through.

1.2 Hand landmark model

  File:     models/hand_landmarker.task  (float16, revision 1; 7,819,105 bytes;
            MD5 15318430ea3851670fe9914116a9cfad)
  Origin:   https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/hand_landmarker/hand_landmarker/float16/1/hand_landmarker.task
  Contents: a zip archive of two TensorFlow Lite models, hand_detector.tflite
            and hand_landmarks_detector.tflite (both dated 2023-04-26).
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0, as stated by Google's model card "MediaPipe
            Hands (Lite/Full)", page 2, section "Licensed under":
            https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-assets/Model%20Card%20Hand%20Tracking%20(Lite_Full)%20with%20Fairness%20Oct%202021.pdf
            Google's Hand Landmarker documentation links to that card:
            https://developers.google.com/edge/mediapipe/solutions/vision/hand_landmarker
  Caveats:  Stated by the model card only. The .task file carries no licence
            text and the download location serves none, so that this card
            covers this exact file rests on Google's documentation linking
            them. The Hand Landmarker page itself states no licence for the
            model (its footer licences the page: CC BY 4.0, with code samples
            under Apache 2.0). The card also says the model was trained on
            limited datasets and is meant for experimental usage, and is not
            intended for human life-critical decisions.

1.3 Licence text: public/mediapipe/LICENSE-mediapipe.txt is a copy of the
    upstream LICENSE (Apache License 2.0). The extra notice at its end
    applies to files under the upstream text-task directory
    (tasks/cc/text/language_detector/...), not to the vision build.


