3.1 js-aruco2

  The app runs js-aruco2's src/aruco.js and src/cv.js in the browser
  (printed-sheet marker detection and the bank-card check). Their headers carry
  an MIT notice with the text below (aruco.js: Damiano Falcioni 2020 and Juan
  Mellado 2011; cv.js: Juan Mellado 2011). The package's LICENSE.txt also
  carries entries for four other works that js-aruco2 is derived from or refers
  to. For OpenCV (BSD-style), AForge.NET (GNU LGPL v3) and StackBoxBlur (MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2010 Mario Klingemann) it reproduces the licence text. For ArUco
  it has only a heading ("BSD License") and no text; the ArUco licence text is
  the one in section 2.1, taken from the header of the dictionary file. The AForge.NET
  reference sits in src/posit2.js, which Open_Mouse does not import. StackBoxBlur
  is code that runs: CV.adaptiveThreshold in cv.js calls CV.stackBoxBlur, and the
  marker detector in aruco.js calls CV.adaptiveThreshold (cv.js cites "Stack
  Blur: Fast But Goodlooking" as its reference). Which parts of aruco.js and
  cv.js derive from ArUco or OpenCV was not confirmed, so the OpenCV notice is
  reproduced here as well, and the StackBoxBlur notice follows it.

